    // The `u8[]` backing `(array (mut i8))` — the emitter's first packed storage type: `0x78` is
    // not a valtype at all, only legal in an array element or struct field, one byte per element
    // instead of the four an i32 array spends. The consequence every read site must honour: `array.get` is invalid on this type — the engine refuses the module, since a byte read must say how it extends. `fbArrayGet` dispatches to `array.get_u` off this heap index.
    wU8(94)  // 0x5e array
    wU8(120) // 0x78 i8 PACKED storagetype
    wU8(1)   // mutable
